lifeos-nix patch f2 — Skip runtime `bun install` in DeployCore (deps are Nix-vendored)

PROBLEM
  `LifeOS/Tools/DeployCore.ts` runs `bun install` in configRoot at activation time,
  reaching the npm registry from a user machine at first launch (RedTeam CR-3).

ROOT CAUSE
  Upstream's AI-native install assumes deps are fetched at activation; Nix packaging
  requires all deps resolved at build time (fixed-output derivations, offline).

SCOPE
  Touches only DeployCore.ts. All five node_modules trees are vendored into the store
  by the derivation and bridged into configRoot by the `lifeos` launcher, so the
  runtime install step is dead weight + an egress hole; replaced with a no-op action.

VERIFICATION
  ISC-133 egress test: full DeployCore activation chain in a deny-all rootless netns
  with strace — zero external connect() attempts, activation exit 0. Build green.

Generated via `diff -u` against pristine 7.1.1 src.

--- a/LifeOS/Tools/DeployCore.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/Tools/DeployCore.ts
@@ -153,13 +153,11 @@
   const { copied, failures } = copyMissing(src, dst);
   r.copied = copied;
   r.failures = failures;
+  // lifeos-nix: runtime `bun install` removed. node_modules are vendored into the Nix
+  // store (fixed-output, reproducible) and symlinked into configRoot by the `lifeos`
+  // launcher — so the install stays fully offline and never touches the npm registry.
   if (failures.length === 0) {
-    const proc = Bun.spawnSync(["bun", "install"], { cwd: configRoot, stdout: "pipe", stderr: "pipe" });
-    if (proc.exitCode !== 0) {
-      r.failures.push(`bun install --cwd ${configRoot} exited ${proc.exitCode}: ${proc.stderr.toString().trim()}`);
-    } else {
-      r.actions.push(`bun install --cwd ${configRoot}`);
-    }
+    r.actions.push("bun install skipped (Nix-vendored node_modules bridged by launcher)");
   }
   return r;
 }
